thbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{G}{G}","name":"Vivien's Talent","oracle_id":"968f0edb-b81f-465a-84b2-f077af61e51b","oracle_text":"Enchant planeswalker\nEnchanted planeswalker has \"[+1]: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature or land card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\"\nWhenever a nontoken creature you control enters, put a loyalty counter on enchanted planeswalker.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-04-21","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment \u2014 Aura"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"},{"cmc":7.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}{U}{U}{U}","name":"Wisdom of Ages","oracle_id":"d9722ec3-aa5e-4c69-8ff0-cef1b1839fa4","oracle_text":"Return all instant and sorcery cards from your graveyard to your hand. You have no maximum hand size for the rest of the game.\nExile Wisdom of Ages.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":"5","mana_cost":"{3}{G}{G}","name":"Wrenn and Seven","oracle_id":"63a509ea-cedc-40e9-b4e8-0ff4fc356485","oracle_text":"+1: Reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\n0: Put any number of land cards from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.\n\u22123: Create a green Treefolk creature token with reach and \"This token's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.\"\n\u22128: Return all permanent cards from your graveyard to your hand. You get an emblem with \"You have no maximum hand size.\"","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-01-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Legendary Planeswalker \u2014 Wrenn"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Copying a loyalty ability doesn't cause any loyalty counters to be added to or removed from the enchanted planeswalker.","oracle_id":"0af6f3ce-59e8-4797-aa1b-dbdb5288fe3d","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate one loyalty ability of each planeswalker you control during each of your turns, whether that ability is one it always has or the one it gains because of Rowan's Talent.","oracle_id":"0af6f3ce-59e8-4797-aa1b-dbdb5288fe3d","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Nettlevine Blight grants the triggered ability to the enchanted permanent, so \u201cyou\u201d refers to that permanent\u2019s controller. The ability will trigger at the end of that player\u2019s turn, and that player chooses the new creature or land to attach Nettlevine Blight to. The player must choose a creature or land they control.","oracle_id":"11132bbe-985d-44fa-a5b4-4b4e0dc3a7cf","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"For a spell with {X} in its mana cost, use the value chosen for X to determine its mana value. For example, Clash of Wills is an instant spell with mana cost {X}{U}. If you chose 2 as the value of X, then Clash of Wills has mana value 3, and Metallurgic Summonings's ability will create a 3/3 token.","oracle_id":"7d5149c6-0e7e-438c-a554-5235c85e2426","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Metallurgic Summonings's first ability resolves and the spell that caused it to trigger has been countered, use that spell's mana value as it last existed on the stack to determine the value of X.","oracle_id":"7d5149c6-0e7e-438c-a554-5235c85e2426","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Metallurgic Summonings's first ability resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger.","oracle_id":"7d5149c6-0e7e-438c-a554-5235c85e2426","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The number of artifacts you control is checked only as you activate Metallurgic Summonings's last ability. It's not checked again as it resolves.","oracle_id":"7d5149c6-0e7e-438c-a554-5235c85e2426","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects modify your hand size, apply them in timestamp order. For example, if you put Null Profusion (an enchantment that says your maximum hand size is two) onto the battlefield and then resolve Praetor's Counsel, you have no maximum hand size. However, if those events happened in the opposite order, your maximum hand size would be two.","oracle_id":"83d8eda7-b8d2-479a-b1ec-de56833a3182","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Later effects that modify your maximum hand size, but don't set it to a specific number, will have no effect.","oracle_id":"83d8eda7-b8d2-479a-b1ec-de56833a3182","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability of Liliana's Talent will trigger whenever a creature deals any damage to the enchanted planeswalker, not just combat damage.","oracle_id":"8c55039d-1303-420c-8547-ebdffb63bf89","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate one loyalty ability of each planeswalker you control during each of your turns, whether that ability is one it always has or the one it gains because of Liliana's Talent.","oracle_id":"8c55039d-1303-420c-8547-ebdffb63bf89","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell's mana value is determined only by its mana cost. Ignore any alternative costs, additional costs, cost increases, or cost reductions.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As the activated ability resolves, it creates a continuous effect that won't begin to apply until the targeted player starts casting a spell this turn. It applies to that spell and the timestamp of that effect is the time that the spell was put on the stack.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cascade triggers when you cast the spell, meaning that it resolves before that spell. If you end up casting the exiled card, it will go on the stack above the spell with cascade.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell has multiple instances of cascade, each one triggers separately.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell with cascade is countered, the cascade ability will still resolve normally.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a card \"without paying its mana cost,\" you can't choose to cast it for any alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs. If the card has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those to cast the card.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some cards, such as modal double-faced cards or adventurer cards, can be cast as one of two different spells, each with different mana costs. If the card you're casting as the cascade ability resolves is one of those cards, you may choose to cast it as either of those spells that has a lower mana value than the spell with cascade.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana value of a split card is determined by the combined mana cost of its two halves. If cascade allows you to cast a split card, you may cast either half but not both halves.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When the cascade ability resolves, you must exile cards. The only optional part of the ability is whether or not you cast the last card exiled.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You exile the cards face up. All players will be able to see them.","oracle_id":"8f351961-69e3-4637-b010-d13f19daca39","published_at":"2023-10-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate one loyalty ability of each planeswalker you control during each of your turns, whether that ability is one it always has or the one it gains because of Vivien's Talent.","oracle_id":"968f0edb-b81f-465a-84b2-f077af61e51b","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability will resolve before the loyalty ability that caused it to trigger. Notably, if that loyalty ability creates creature tokens, those creatures won't be on the battlefield yet to get +2/+2 and gain vigilance.","oracle_id":"969b81d2-e95b-4a3f-9548-9394e3a6727e","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The set of creatures affected by Elspeth's Talent's last ability is determined as the ability resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn and noncreature permanents that become creatures later in the turn won't get +2/+2 and gain vigilance.","oracle_id":"969b81d2-e95b-4a3f-9548-9394e3a6727e","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate one loyalty ability of each planeswalker you control during each of your turns, whether that ability is one it always has or the one it gains because of Elspeth's Talent.","oracle_id":"969b81d2-e95b-4a3f-9548-9394e3a6727e","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Which creature cards to return to your hand is determined as Garna's triggered ability resolves. If Garna somehow finds its way into your graveyard before that, perhaps due to the \"legend rule,\" it will be returned to your hand.","oracle_id":"97cb993c-90ae-49ff-8ccb-b4fe317a43ef","published_at":"2018-12-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the enchanted artifact has X in its mana cost, X is 0.","oracle_id":"af8fba92-f7e5-485d-a1da-a30c46a3992e","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mana cost includes any requirements for colored mana, although most artifacts don\u2019t have any color requirements.","oracle_id":"af8fba92-f7e5-485d-a1da-a30c46a3992e","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When this ability resolves, it returns all creature cards currently in your graveyard that were put there directly from the battlefield sometime during the turn. This includes cards that were put into your graveyard before Gleancrawler entered the battlefield.","oracle_id":"bb7389fa-ab01-4ca2-bd18-03cf5b4cedf6","published_at":"2005-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you sacrifice No Rest for the Wicked on the same turn you cast it, all creature cards that were put into your graveyard from the battlefield that turn will be returned to your hand, including any that were put into your graveyard before No Rest for the Wicked entered the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d03fd358-ff3f-45ab-9601-07dbb535cb51","published_at":"2007-07-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It doesn\u2019t matter who controlled the creature cards when they were on the battlefield. As long as they were put into your graveyard, you get to put them into your hand.","oracle_id":"d03fd358-ff3f-45ab-9601-07dbb535cb51","published_at":"2007-07-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate one loyalty ability of each planeswalker you control during each of your turns, whether that ability is one it always has or the one it gains because of Teferi's Talent.","oracle_id":"efc23669-1bbb-487f-94b3-cc07f3cd35f6","published_at":"2023-04-14","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
